QUERY: rg -n -i '^description:.*(requirement|objective|diagnostic|observab|fixed.*decomposition|bounded.*adapt)' kb/theory/ --glob *.md --glob !*.brief.md
kb/theory/a-proximate-target-is-checked-for-achievement-not-for-warrant.md:2:description: "Between an improvement objective and its oracles sits a target level — a property pursued because it is held to serve the objective — whose linking claim no check in the loop evaluates"
kb/theory/clear-instructions-can-compose-into-an-unsettled-contract.md:2:description: "Uses a JSON-only rule and a general exception rule to show how scope and precedence can leave combined requirements unsettled, even when each instruction has a clear ordinary use."
kb/theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md:2:description: "Why optimization cannot repair consequential distinctions, responses, or mappings outside the effective update space of a fixed task decomposition"
kb/theory/agent-memory-needs-discoverable-composable-trusted-knowledge-under.md:2:description: "Distinguishes four use-time requirements for remembered knowledge—discoverability, loadability, composability, and calibrated trust—from system-level activation."
kb/theory/a-guard-against-a-conjectured-requirement-removes-the-experiment-that.md:2:description: "A guard against an unstated requirement holds the condition at the value where the conjecture and its negation agree, so it immunizes the conjecture; explains why test-selected agents guard by default and when omitting is the cheaper experiment"
kb/theory/designing-agent-memory-systems.md:2:description: "Derives agent-memory design pressures and links to a requirements inventory for agents designing or evaluating memory systems"
kb/theory/progressive-constraining-commits-only-after-patterns-stabilize.md:2:description: "Progressive extraction uses repeated behavior to identify stable candidates, then checks the extracted rule against the applicable requirement before committing it."
kb/theory/scenario-decomposition-drives-architecture.md:2:description: Deriving architectural requirements by decomposing concrete user stories into step-by-step context needs — not from abstract read/write operations but from what the agent actually has to load at each stage
kb/theory/agents-navigate-by-deciding-what-to-read-next.md:2:description: "Models agent navigation as repeated follow/skip judgment under bounded context: cue diagnosticity must repay its own context cost, so longer pointer context is not automatically better"
kb/theory/holding-the-client-fixed-exports-the-least-warrantable-decisions.md:2:description: "A fixed-client benchmark measures worker capability; it leaves broader closure untested when the client supplies internal production decisions, while ordinary user requirements and acceptance may remain external"
kb/theory/ad-hoc-prompts-extend-the-system-without-schema-changes.md:2:description: Any system with an LLM agent layer can absorb new requirements through natural language prompts without changing the deterministic base
kb/theory/technical-constraints-make-kb-objective-choice-engineering.md:2:description: "Three technical constraints and the codification lever make KB objective-function choice testable engineering, not philosophy; goals set the loss, local contracts specialize it, and oracle strength differs by objective"
kb/theory/link-following-and-search-impose-different-metadata-requirements.md:2:description: Compares contextual local steps with long-range search and explains why these recurring navigation modes impose different metadata requirements on an agent knowledge base
kb/theory/symbolic-form-holds-consumers-to-a-semantic-reference.md:2:description: "Explains why adopting a pinned model can codify a prompt without formalizing English, and separates reference conformance, permitted variation, opacity, and requirement adequacy."
kb/theory/verifiability-gradient.md:2:description: Compare verification by the requirement checked, reset conditions, retry cost and strength of feedback; prompts and code have no automatic ordering on these dimensions
kb/theory/changing-requirements-conflate-genuine-change-with-disambiguation.md:2:description: "Separates world change from late discovery that downstream work chose the wrong interpretation of an underspecified requirement; short iterations mainly limit propagation of the latter"
kb/theory/definitions/self-improving-system.md:2:description: "Definition — operative, evidence-responsive change to a system's own behavior-determining organization, read against a declared boundary, horizon, and improvement objective"
kb/theory/prompting-changes-failure-diagnosis-with-the-semantic-reference.md:2:description: "Two accounts of prompting share a behavior-prediction problem but assign failures differently: English governs requirements, or an adopted model package defines the prompt language."
kb/theory/definitions/evidence-bearing-on-an-improvement-objective.md:2:description: "Definition — evidence bears on an improvement objective when it carries information about the criterion: gradients, rewards, errors, viability signals, tests, judgments; no evaluator required"
kb/theory/factory-learning-is-experience-responsive-retention-that-improves.md:2:description: "Experience-responsive retention: production experience determines a retained change to reusable family machinery that later production depends on; factory-level learning is retention that improves the factory relative to a declared objective"
kb/theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md:2:description: "An artifact can exactly implement a requirement while the requirement remains a conjectured proxy for a declared objective; assess each named path separately, and attribute failure to the link without erasing local correctness"
kb/theory/silent-disambiguation-is-the-semantic-analogue-of-tool-fallback.md:2:description: When an agent silently resolves unacknowledged material ambiguity in a spec, final success hides that the contract failed to determine the path — an extension of the tool-fallback observability problem
kb/theory/revising-an-improvement-objective-is-licensed-from-outside-it.md:2:description: "Objective change is improvement only against a level outside both objectives; proxy revision, re-indexing, and surfaced under-specification subtract most apparent cases"
kb/theory/residue-classes-need-different-mechanisms-so-architecture-is-mixed.md:2:description: "Different reasons for an untransferred decision identify different missing functions; a single process can supply several, and the current carrier split is not a permanent requirement"
kb/theory/agent-memory-requirements/README.md:2:description: "Navigation hub for concrete agent-memory requirements extracted from the memory-system design synthesis"
kb/theory/programming-practices-for-prompts-need-question-specific-evidence.md:2:description: "Maps typing, testing, code extraction and versioning to the questions they answer; distinguishes requirement adequacy, conformance, predictive fidelity and execution variation."
kb/theory/agent-memory-requirements/adaptation-survey-corroborates-memory-requirements.md:2:description: "The agentic-adaptation survey supports the memory requirements map by treating memory and skills as adaptive tools, but it needs substrate, form, lineage, and authority governance to become design guidance"
kb/theory/evaluation-automation-is-phase-gated-by-comprehension.md:2:description: Optimization loops need diagnostic error analysis and demonstrated judge discrimination before automation can improve behavior rather than just score
kb/theory/self-improvement-is-relative-to-a-declared-objective.md:2:description: "The improvement objective is a declared parameter alongside boundary and horizon, carrying two separable conditions — indexed by the analyst, antecedent in the pathway — whose failures differ in kind"
kb/theory/llm-output-deviation-requires-three-way-diagnosis.md:2:description: "For a fixed assembled input, whether V exceeds I, whether D escapes V, and how D's spread affects realization are three diagnostic questions with different primary repair surfaces"
kb/theory/a-claim-without-external-assessment-carries-three-obligations.md:2:description: "Without external assessment a claim needs its own contradiction-and-support rule, a comparison level for objective change, and a performance measure it does not grade itself, plus attribution when it asserts a cause"

EXIT: 0
